Here is the critical apparatus collating manuscript Vat. lat. 629 f. 3v (V) against the base text of Chaparro Gómez 1985 (C) for Isidore §37. All scribal anomalies and orthographic variations have been strictly preserved without normalization.

**Apparatus Criticus**

ille] Hic V (substitution) ;
hic] Hic autem V (addition) ;
nobilis] nobili V (substitution) ;
ortus] ortus est V (addition) ;
in] *om.* V (omission) ;
atrocique] atroque V (substitution / scribal anomaly) ;
extincxit] extinxit V (orthographic) ;

*Philological Note:* The reading *atroque* in V is preserved exactly as transcribed; it is a clear scribal anomaly (likely a haplography or morphological confusion for *atrocique*), but must not be normalized. The orthographic variation between the base text's *extincxit* and V's *extinxit* is likewise retained precisely as it appears in the manuscript witness. No lacunae are present in this specific collation sample.
